Subject: best way for inspection of a data frame within RApache
Message-ID: <x2YUYEPzHvk.o5A_mEB62M0J@rapache.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rapache/c/x2YUYEPzHvk/m/o5A_mEB62M0J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi folks -

I'm looking for a quick & dirty way to inspect data frames that I'm passing around within RApache.  Right now, this is my function (below), which doesn't perform particularly well.  Any thoughts on a better way?

Thanks!

Mike

displayData <- function(df) {
  setContentType('text/html')
  cat('<html><body><table>')
  for (i in 1:dim(df)[1]) {
    cat('<tr>')
    for (j in 1:length(df[i,])) {
      cat('<td>')
      if (!(is.na <http://is.na>(df[i,j]))) {
        cat(as.character(df[i,j]))
      }
      cat('</td>')
    }
    cat('</tr>')
  }
  cat('</table></body></html>')

