Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

UPDATE - smooth sailing on Snow Leopard.

./configure worked fine - no need to edit the makefiles to enforce
x86_64 architecture.

Still need to use the option: --with-apache2-apxs=/usr/sbin/apxs.

One difference is that this time I made sure to point toward the R64
binary (64 bit) instead of R (32 bit), since both are installed with
the default MacOS installer.  I suspect this may have been the key all
along.

So the final command was:
./configure --with-apache2-apxs=/usr/sbin/apxs --with-R=/usr/bin/R64
sudo make
sudo make install

No problems.

-b

